ng)\n\nConsider the graph of $y=f(x)$ above. Of the following, which could be the graph of $y={f}^{′}(x)$, the derivative of $f(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice the following:\n\n- At the stationary points, where the tangent line to $y=f(x)$ is parallel to the $x$-axis, we have ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$\n\n- When $f(x)$ is increasing, we have ${f}^{′}(x)>0.$\n\n- When $f(x)$ is decreasing, we have ${f}^{′}(x)<0.$\n\nWe can now summarize the information from the graph in the table below. Note that the stationary point was identified (approximately) from the graph of $y=f(x)$:\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-0.5)$ | $-0.5$ | $(-0.5,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f$ | $↘$ | $\\text{min}$ | $↗$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n\nAdditionally, from the graph of $y=f(x),$ we can conclude that there are no inflection points.  Also, the graph of $y=f(x)$ is concave up in $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ and $y={f}^{′}(x)$ is increasing.\n\nTherefore, the graph of $y={f}^{′}(x)$ may look as shown below.\n\n![](images/60/608c88c65eff4c63520a7a5a4a51a468601b0d6edcf5f063475c8429e1308962.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100929 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa025d7b-74d5-5627-a7cd-12e3681b8b82" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Derivative of a Quadratic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "277a2d03-83e1-5f35-888c-224cc21dd025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/75/75a8103219a95d991891315a5e3ae6c6ac5e938dd1a1601ccc8aafe09004997d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505173} {:answer/id #uuid "3c6f0426-db1f-5cb3-b483-6634da4706fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fde284c6bda2a0a9dba79a41348cf25ce7d5e5db8d2af996c577ceca721d5ab2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505215} {:answer/id #uuid "63581de7-e105-556b-8269-b74a607c6547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/